      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-143529",
      ":question/problem": "A company manufactures electronic components. Of the components manufactured, $45%$ are produced by the first machine, $25%$ are produced by the second machine, and the third machine produces the remaining.\nIf $8%$ of the components produced by the first machine, $4%$ produced by the second machine, and $5%$ produced by the third machine are defective, what is the probability that a randomly selected component is defective?\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
