      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-143749",
      ":question/problem": "Three companies supply widgets to a car shop. Company $A$ supplies $45%$ of the widgets, of which $2%$ are defective. Company $B$ provides $40%$ of the widgets, of which  $3%$ are defective. And company $C$ supplies the remaining widgets, of which $4%$ are defective. What is the probability that a randomly chosen widget from these companies will turn out to be defective?"
